hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27291","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi Ayyub al-Hajari, from Juwayriyah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Juwayriyah on a Friday while she was fasting. He said to her: Did you fast yesterday. She said: No. He said: Will you fast tomorrow. She said: No. He said: Then break."
"27292","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi Ayyub, from Juwayriyah daughter of al-Harith, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her while she was fasting. He said: Did you fast yesterday. She said: No. He said: Do you want to fast tomorrow. She said: No. He said: Then break."
"27293","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from his maternal aunt Umm Uthman, from al-Tufayl, brother's son of Juwayriyah, from Juwayriyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wears a garment of silk, Allah will clothe him a garment of Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"27294","Rawh narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freed slave of the family of Talhah, he said: I heard Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, narrating, from Ibn Abbas, from Juwayriyah daughter of al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me in the morning while I was glorifying, then he left for a need, then he returned near midday and said: You have remained sitting. I said: Yes. He said: Shall I not teach you words, if weighed with them they would equal them, or if measured with them they would outweigh them, meaning with all she glorified: Glory be to Allah, number of His creation, three times; Glory be to Allah, weight of His Throne, three times; Glory be to Allah, pleasure of Himself, three times; Glory be to Allah, ink of His words, three times."
